      "writtenOn": "2025-01-21T18:41:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just raising a design point - the lack of comment support and fairly strict structure of json (e.g. no trailing commas) can be annoying in config files. They were used for `cargo_embargo` originally because it was a python script, and packages were unavailable, so json was one of the few things we could default parse.\n\nIn the Rust world, are you sure you wouldn\u0027t prefer toml?\n\nIt should also support the `serde`-based config structure you\u0027re using, so it would be a minimal code change at this point.",
      "revId": "e65dc45f4de31540a2fc826d93a418cefec86fc3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
