        "id": 1416371
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-21T18:41:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "!!! Danger\n\nThis potentially fetches licenses from the internet. If we need to paste license text into crates for some reason, this should be done from a static resource committed to the android repo.",
      "revId": "e65dc45f4de31540a2fc826d93a418cefec86fc3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fbf3213c_9ca3ea32",
        "filename": "tools/external_crates/crate_tool/src/managed_crate.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 334,
      "author": {
        "id": 1903830
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-21T18:48:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s basically what we\u0027re already doing with patch files.\n\nWe are already fetching crates from the internet; this doesn\u0027t seem significantly different or worse. It also gives us the provenance of the license file.\n\nI\u0027d really like to reduce the number of patch files we are keeping around.\n\nI guess another way to do this would be to add a \"preserve\" block to the config file, indicating \"this file is not present in the crate, but keep it around when regenerating/upgrading\".",
      "parentUuid": "39e8f720_4059c55f",
      "revId": "e65dc45f4de31540a2fc826d93a418cefec86fc3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9b52e131_a00e9e50",
        "filename": "tools/external_crates/crate_tool/src/managed_crate.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 334,
      "author": {
        "id": 1416371
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-21T18:59:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In theory, all the license files should be one of a small number of enumerated licenses. IIRC add3prf.py used to be able to generate those for you based on the Cargo license. Could we do something similar here?\n\nI understand wanting to decrease the patchfile count, I was suggesting having \"APACHE2.0\" and \"MIT\", etc. packaged somewhere in the development tools, and just fetching from there rather than the internet.",
      "parentUuid": "fbf3213c_9ca3ea32",
      "revId": "e65dc45f4de31540a2fc826d93a418cefec86fc3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "18a4da72_00a0fe1b",
        "filename": "tools/external_crates/crate_tool/src/managed_crate.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 334,
      "author": {
        "id": 1416371
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-21T19:07:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe it makes sense to split this into a separate patch unles Stephen wants to step in and say that he thinks this isn\u0027t scary? The rest of the change LGTM.",
      "parentUuid": "9b52e131_a00e9e50",
      "revId": "e65dc45f4de31540a2fc826d93a418cefec86fc3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cbd8b1f2_5af535d2",
        "filename": "tools/external_crates/crate_tool/src/managed_crate.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 334,
      "author": {
        "id": 1903830
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-21T19:16:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "One thing we would lose with just using boilerplate text is copyright notices.\n\nFor example, https://github.com/stepancheg/rust-protobuf/blob/master/LICENSE.txt for crates/protobuf-json-mapping is an MIT license file. Per https://opensource.org/license/mit, it\u0027s supposed to start with Copyright \u003cYEAR\u003e \u003cCOPYRIGHT HOLDER\u003e\n\nhttps://opensource.org/license/apache-2-0 states that Apache-2.0 license are also supposed to mention the copyright holder.\n\nAll else being equal (which is never the case), it seems better to have the *actual* license file.",
      "parentUuid": "9b52e131_a00e9e50",
      "revId": "e65dc45f4de31540a2fc826d93a418cefec86fc3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8acf5fb3_69ad7b28",
        "filename": "tools/external_crates/crate_tool/src/managed_crate.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 334,
      "author": {
        "id": 1010056
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-21T19:17:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m only getting back to the office now, but I generally prefer more patches with independent things, rather than a few things rolled into a single CL. This part seems a bit contentious and I don\u0027t think I\u0027m fully understanding the implications of the network aspect yet, so maybe splitting is the best option.",
      "parentUuid": "18a4da72_00a0fe1b",
      "revId": "e65dc45f4de31540a2fc826d93a418cefec86fc3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
